IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `pa-pit`

-- Pennsylvania Tax Reform Code of 1971, Article III (personal income tax) -- the seat of the individual taxpayer.
-- "Am I a Pennsylvania resident? Must I file? How much tax do I owe? Do I qualify for Tax Forgiveness? What do I get for
-- tax I paid to another state? What is left to pay, or to come back?"
--
-- Every question calls the core in pa-pit.l4; no rule is restated here. Each input is one fact the person can state.
-- Facts the Article borrows (IRC s 151 dependants, the federal return due date) or leaves to detail (which class an
-- amount falls in, what is "poverty income") are asked as facts.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Pennsylvania personal income tax -- the taxpayer's questions`

§§ `Questions this encoding does not cover`

DECLARE `Why not covered` IS ONE OF
    `a part-year resident's tax is not encoded (the year is split between the resident and nonresident rules of s 302(a) and (b) by department regulation, not deposited)`

GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH A TYPE
DECLARE `Answer` a IS ONE OF
    `answered`    HAS `the answer` IS AN a
    `not covered` HAS `because`    IS A `Why not covered`

DECLARE `My residence status for the year` IS ONE OF
    `resident for the whole taxable year`
    `nonresident for the whole taxable year`
    `resident for part of the taxable year`

GIVEN `compensation` IS A NUMBER
      `net profits` IS A NUMBER
      `property gains` IS A NUMBER
      `rents and royalties` IS A NUMBER
      `dividends` IS A NUMBER
      `interest` IS A NUMBER
      `gambling and lottery winnings` IS A NUMBER
      `estate or trust income` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `Income by class`
`my income by class` `compensation` `net profits` `property gains` `rents and royalties` `dividends` `interest` `gambling and lottery winnings` `estate or trust income` MEANS
    `Income by class` WITH
        `compensation`                                              IS `compensation`
        `net profits`                                               IS `net profits`
        `net gains or income from disposition of property`          IS `property gains`
        `net gains or income from rents, royalties, patents and copyrights` IS `rents and royalties`
        `dividends`                                                 IS `dividends`
        `interest`                                                  IS `interest`
        `gambling and lottery winnings`                             IS `gambling and lottery winnings`
        `net gains or income derived through estates or trusts`     IS `estate or trust income`

§§ `Am I a resident (s 301(p))`

@export Am I a "resident individual" of Pennsylvania for the taxable year under s 301(p) of the Tax Reform Code of 1971?
GIVEN `I am domiciled in Pennsylvania` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether Pennsylvania is your domicile (your true, fixed, permanent home, to which you intend to return)
      `I keep a permanent place of abode in Pennsylvania` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you maintain a permanent place to live in Pennsylvania during the year
      `I keep a permanent place of abode outside Pennsylvania` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you maintain a permanent place to live outside Pennsylvania during the year
      `days I spent in Pennsylvania` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days of the taxable year, in total, you spent in Pennsylvania
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I a Pennsylvania resident individual` IF
    `is a resident individual` `I am domiciled in Pennsylvania` `I keep a permanent place of abode in Pennsylvania` `I keep a permanent place of abode outside Pennsylvania` `days I spent in Pennsylvania`

§§ `Must I file a return, and by when (ss 330(a), 332)`

DECLARE `Must I file` IS ONE OF
    `yes: I have income in a class, so I must file a return, and pay any tax due, by the day my federal income tax return is due or would be due (ss 330(a), 332)`
    `no: I have no income in any class of s 303 for the year, so s 330(a) does not require a return`

@export Must I file a Pennsylvania personal income tax return for the year?
GIVEN `compensation` IS A NUMBER @desc Your compensation for the year in US dollars: salaries, wages, commissions, bonuses, tips and similar pay (s 303(a)(1)); for a nonresident, only Pennsylvania-source amounts
      `net profits` IS A NUMBER @desc Net profits (or a net loss, as a negative number) from a business, profession or farm, in US dollars (s 303(a)(2)); for a nonresident, Pennsylvania-source only
      `property gains` IS A NUMBER @desc Net gains (or a net loss, negative) from selling or exchanging property, in US dollars (s 303(a)(3)); for a nonresident, Pennsylvania-source only
      `rents and royalties` IS A NUMBER @desc Net income (or a net loss, negative) from rents, royalties, patents and copyrights, in US dollars (s 303(a)(4)); for a nonresident, Pennsylvania-source only
      `dividends` IS A NUMBER @desc Dividends received, in US dollars (s 303(a)(5)); for a nonresident, Pennsylvania-source only
      `interest` IS A NUMBER @desc Taxable interest, other than interest on obligations that are free of state tax, in US dollars (s 303(a)(6)); for a nonresident, Pennsylvania-source only
      `gambling and lottery winnings` IS A NUMBER @desc Gambling and lottery winnings, other than noncash Pennsylvania State Lottery prizes, in US dollars (s 303(a)(7)); for a nonresident, Pennsylvania-source only
      `estate or trust income` IS A NUMBER @desc Net income (or a net loss, negative) received through estates or trusts, in US dollars (s 303(a)(8)); for a nonresident, Pennsylvania-source only
GIVETH A `Must I file`
`Must I file a Pennsylvania return` MEANS
    IF `has income for the taxable year` (`my income by class` `compensation` `net profits` `property gains` `rents and royalties` `dividends` `interest` `gambling and lottery winnings` `estate or trust income`)
    THEN `yes: I have income in a class, so I must file a return, and pay any tax due, by the day my federal income tax return is due or would be due (ss 330(a), 332)`
    ELSE `no: I have no income in any class of s 303 for the year, so s 330(a) does not require a return`

§§ `How much tax is imposed (ss 302, 303)`

@export How much Pennsylvania personal income tax is imposed on my income for the year, before credits and Tax Forgiveness?
GIVEN `my residence status` IS A `My residence status for the year` @desc Whether you were a Pennsylvania resident for the whole year, a nonresident for the whole year, or a resident for part of it
      `compensation` IS A NUMBER @desc Your compensation for the year in US dollars (s 303(a)(1)); for a nonresident, Pennsylvania-source only
      `net profits` IS A NUMBER @desc Net profits or loss (negative) from a business, profession or farm, in US dollars (s 303(a)(2))
      `property gains` IS A NUMBER @desc Net gains or loss (negative) from disposing of property, in US dollars (s 303(a)(3))
      `rents and royalties` IS A NUMBER @desc Net income or loss (negative) from rents, royalties, patents and copyrights, in US dollars (s 303(a)(4))
      `dividends` IS A NUMBER @desc Dividends, in US dollars (s 303(a)(5))
      `interest` IS A NUMBER @desc Taxable interest, in US dollars (s 303(a)(6))
      `gambling and lottery winnings` IS A NUMBER @desc Gambling and lottery winnings, in US dollars (s 303(a)(7))
      `estate or trust income` IS A NUMBER @desc Net income or loss (negative) through estates or trusts, in US dollars (s 303(a)(8))
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`How much Pennsylvania tax is imposed on me` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my residence status`
    WHEN `resident for part of the taxable year` THEN `not covered` `a part-year resident's tax is not encoded (the year is split between the resident and nonresident rules of s 302(a) and (b) by department regulation, not deposited)`
    OTHERWISE `answered` (`the tax imposed` (`my income by class` `compensation` `net profits` `property gains` `rents and royalties` `dividends` `interest` `gambling and lottery winnings` `estate or trust income`))

§§ `Tax Forgiveness (s 304)`

@export What share of my Pennsylvania income tax is forgiven under the special tax provisions for poverty (Tax Forgiveness, s 304)?
GIVEN `someone else can claim me as a dependent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a dependent of another taxpayer for federal income tax purposes (IRC s 151)
      `I am married` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were married at the end of the taxable year
      `my spouse and I file separate returns` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If married, whether you and your spouse file separate Pennsylvania returns
      `we lived apart for the last six months of the year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If married, whether you and your spouse lived apart at all times during the last six months of the taxable year
      `we are separated under a written agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If married, whether you and your spouse are separated under a written separation agreement
      `my poverty income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your poverty income for the whole year in US dollars (yours and your spouse's together if you count as married): all money and property received, including tax-exempt interest, but not Social Security, retirement benefits, unemployment compensation, public assistance, workers' compensation, sickness or disability payments, reimbursed expenses or combat pay (s 301(o.2))
      `my number of dependent children` IS A NUMBER @desc How many children are your dependents for federal income tax purposes (IRC s 151)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What share of my tax is forgiven` MEANS
    `the special tax provisions share` `someone else can claim me as a dependent` `my poverty income` (`is a married claimant for s 304` `I am married` `my spouse and I file separate returns` `we lived apart for the last six months of the year` `we are separated under a written agreement`) `my number of dependent children`

@export What is the most poverty income I can have and still have all of my Pennsylvania income tax forgiven (s 304(d)(1))?
GIVEN `I am married` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were married at the end of the taxable year
      `my spouse and I file separate returns` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If married, whether you and your spouse file separate Pennsylvania returns
      `we lived apart for the last six months of the year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If married, whether you lived apart at all times during the last six months of the year
      `we are separated under a written agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If married, whether you are separated under a written separation agreement
      `my number of dependent children` IS A NUMBER @desc How many children are your dependents for federal income tax purposes (IRC s 151)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`The most poverty income for full forgiveness` MEANS
    `the poverty income limitation` (`is a married claimant for s 304` `I am married` `my spouse and I file separate returns` `we lived apart for the last six months of the year` `we are separated under a written agreement`) `my number of dependent children`

§§ `Tax paid to another state (s 314)`

-- Only where the person paid income tax to another state on income Pennsylvania also taxes.
@export As a Pennsylvania resident, how much credit do I get for income tax I paid to another state (s 314)?
GIVEN `my residence status` IS A `My residence status for the year` @desc Whether you were a Pennsylvania resident for the whole year, a nonresident for the whole year, or a resident for part of it
      `tax imposed on me` IS A NUMBER @desc The Pennsylvania tax imposed on your income, in US dollars (the answer to the question about the tax imposed)
      `my total taxable income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your total Pennsylvania taxable income for the year, in US dollars
      `income taxed by the other state` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of that income the other state also taxed, in US dollars
      `tax paid to the other state` IS A NUMBER @desc The income tax the other state imposed on you on that income, in US dollars
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`My credit for tax paid to another state` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my residence status`
    WHEN `resident for the whole taxable year` THEN `answered` (`the credit for tax paid to another state` `tax imposed on me` `tax paid to the other state` `income taxed by the other state` `my total taxable income`)
    WHEN `nonresident for the whole taxable year` THEN `answered` 0
    WHEN `resident for part of the taxable year` THEN `not covered` `a part-year resident's tax is not encoded (the year is split between the resident and nonresident rules of s 302(a) and (b) by department regulation, not deposited)`

§§ `What is left to pay, or to come back (ss 312, 314, 304)`

@export How much Pennsylvania personal income tax do I still owe for the year (a negative answer is an overpayment to come back)?
GIVEN `my residence status` IS A `My residence status for the year` @desc Whether you were a Pennsylvania resident for the whole year, a nonresident for the whole year, or a resident for part of it
      `compensation` IS A NUMBER @desc Your compensation for the year in US dollars (s 303(a)(1)); for a nonresident, Pennsylvania-source only
      `net profits` IS A NUMBER @desc Net profits or loss (negative) from a business, profession or farm, in US dollars (s 303(a)(2))
      `property gains` IS A NUMBER @desc Net gains or loss (negative) from disposing of property, in US dollars (s 303(a)(3))
      `rents and royalties` IS A NUMBER @desc Net income or loss (negative) from rents, royalties, patents and copyrights, in US dollars (s 303(a)(4))
      `dividends` IS A NUMBER @desc Dividends, in US dollars (s 303(a)(5))
      `interest` IS A NUMBER @desc Taxable interest, in US dollars (s 303(a)(6))
      `gambling and lottery winnings` IS A NUMBER @desc Gambling and lottery winnings, in US dollars (s 303(a)(7))
      `estate or trust income` IS A NUMBER @desc Net income or loss (negative) through estates or trusts, in US dollars (s 303(a)(8))
      `income taxed by the other state` IS A NUMBER @desc If a resident, how much of your income another state also taxed, in US dollars (0 if none)
      `tax paid to the other state` IS A NUMBER @desc If a resident, the income tax another state imposed on that income, in US dollars (0 if none)
      `someone else can claim me as a dependent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a dependent of another taxpayer for federal income tax purposes (IRC s 151)
      `I am married` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were married at the end of the taxable year
      `my spouse and I file separate returns` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If married, whether you and your spouse file separate Pennsylvania returns
      `we lived apart for the last six months of the year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If married, whether you lived apart at all times during the last six months of the year
      `we are separated under a written agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If married, whether you are separated under a written separation agreement
      `my poverty income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your poverty income for the whole year in US dollars (joint with your spouse if you count as married), as defined in s 301(o.2)
      `my number of dependent children` IS A NUMBER @desc How many children are your dependents for federal income tax purposes (IRC s 151)
      `tax withheld and estimated tax I paid` IS A NUMBER @desc Pennsylvania income tax withheld from your pay and estimated tax you paid for the year, in US dollars
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`How much Pennsylvania tax do I still owe` MEANS
    CONSIDER `How much Pennsylvania tax is imposed on me` `my residence status` `compensation` `net profits` `property gains` `rents and royalties` `dividends` `interest` `gambling and lottery winnings` `estate or trust income`
    WHEN `not covered` r THEN `not covered` r
    WHEN `answered` `the tax` THEN
        CONSIDER `My credit for tax paid to another state` `my residence status` `the tax` (`the income taxed` (`my income by class` `compensation` `net profits` `property gains` `rents and royalties` `dividends` `interest` `gambling and lottery winnings` `estate or trust income`)) `income taxed by the other state` `tax paid to the other state`
        WHEN `not covered` r2 THEN `not covered` r2
        WHEN `answered` `the credit` THEN
            `answered` (`the balance due` `the tax` `the credit` (`What share of my tax is forgiven` `someone else can claim me as a dependent` `I am married` `my spouse and I file separate returns` `we lived apart for the last six months of the year` `we are separated under a written agreement` `my poverty income` `my number of dependent children`) `tax withheld and estimated tax I paid`)
